  %article.club-report
    %h3= "Trad Beyond the Basics class, extra climbing day and an unexpected rave - Snowshed Tahoe - Aug 22nd, 2026"
    = link_to "View photos", "https://photos.app.goo.gl/59ZYBsK4EEgtQG1ZA", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener"
    %details.club-report-details
      %summary Read trip report
      .club-report-copy
        %p= "A crew of cragmont clubbers capitalized on a climbing class coupon! Erik, the owner of Vertical Pursuits, hooked us up with a discounted Trad Beyond the Basics course which promised to raise our trad leading levels from 5.low to 5.high. And it did!"
        %p= "David and Jessica arrived a day early and spied a colorful rave bubbling beneath the bridge. Being the community minded climbers they are, they set up a rappelling station and started handing out free rides to adventurous partygoers."
        %p= "Scott and I arrived the next morning and met them, along with Erik and one other student, at Snowshed Wall in Donner Summit. We spent the day working on three trad routes in the best corner of the crag. Erik seemed to know every single other climber there - the vibe was that of a backyard BBQ but with more ropes."
        %p= "We started with some mock leads on a 5.6 and a 5.9, followed by some true leading after Erik inspected our gear placements. After I led the 5.6, Erik suggested I try the 5.10b on top rope. Feeling a bit intimiated, I gave it a shot and fell a couple of times, but made it to the top in one piece. I did not feel confident that I could lead it, but Erik hyped me up until there I was, leading a 10b - the hardest grade I'd lead up till then was a 5.6. I fell twice and it wasn't even scary - the crux was very well protected and Erik was right there beside me on a static line, sharing the tips, beta, and encouragement I needed. I topped out victorious and only a little bloody, with a new found confidence for working on challenging trad routes without that extra top rope tether."
        %p= "Huge shout out to Erik for sharing his skill, knoweldge, and impeccably good energy with us that Sunday. If you're ever looking for a course, hit him up!"
        %p= "- Nat Baykova"
  %article.club-report
    %h3= "Tuolumne - Aug 14th, 2026"
    = link_to "View photos", "https://photos.app.goo.gl/ZjwHn7mnyJcKiyWw9", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener"
    %details.club-report-details
      %summary Read trip report
      .club-report-copy
        %p= "Finn and I drove into Yosemite on Saturday morning and spent the day at Stately Pleasure Dome. I got to work on gear placement on a 2 pitch 5.3 trad route while David basically walked up the slope beside me and gave me pointers. It was great for building confidence as a trad newbie. Scott W and Finn followed, cleaned, and captured the perfect photo of David enjoying a hands-free, foot-free rest on the slope."
        %p= "Later we joined Kathy, Nick, and Laura in climbing Turkey Trot, Jonah, and Potter in Wonderland. The slabby sport climbs seemed to grow hotter, steeper, and more slippery as the day went on - some of the bolts definitely migrated further apart when we weren't looking."
        %p= "It was a pretty busy crag. A few groups descended from further up the dome, and we watched in fascinated horror as a deeply dysfunctional British family scrambled all over the routes to our right. We spent a good bit of time at the campfire that night trying to puzzle out just what the hell they were doing with those three ropes."
        %p= "On Sunday Scott, David, Finn and I headed to Olmstead Canyon, where we later met up with Rahul and Pasha. This crag felt like a hidden gem - we nearly had the whole place to ourselves, just one other duo showed up."
        %p= "Scott and I practiced aiding a tricky overhung crack route, Tideline, while David and Rahul projected a 12a route to our left, Body Double. Having aided up my route, I tried it on top rope and only got about 1/3 of the way before pumping out. Next thing I know, a super polite climber from the duo mentioned earlier sends the thing with the ease of a practiced dancer. There's nothing like wrestling with a tough climb then watching the coolest, most polite cucumber in the park waltz right up it like a salmon up river. He told me he'd been working on it all season, and had spent about 6 sessions working out the gear placement. It was a beautiful send and filled my cup with inspiration."
        %p= "After that, Scott, Finn and I took turns sacrificing bits of our hands to the deceptively difficult 10a crack climb, Ivory Tower, Center. It was awful, Scott and I both want to come back and project that thing - mostly out of spite."
        %p= "It was a wonderful trip, looking forward to the next one!"
        %p= "- Nat Baykova"
