    %h3= "Guadalupe Rock June 27th, 2026"
    = link_to "View photos", "https://photos.google.com/share/AF1QipMybfCZH-pThKcvZropkwrevjftR2ri89NU006gFXyR8Le0eMcI4sEFjePw9jJ42w?key=MDhRTkdwUVptT2RfQVQ2V2xoOGlBYTB0MWpoS3RR", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener"
    %details.club-report-details
      %summary Read trip report
      .club-report-copy
        %p= "When Castle Rock was rained out, we improvised. Guadalupe Rock is a 45 minute drive east of Castle Rock, and is a hidden gem. A 50 ft boulder sitting pretty in the water flowing from the Guadalupe reservoir."
        %p= "It seems to get a bad rap in the guide books due to varying conditions at the base - you may get your rope wet or your feet muddy depending on the water level. For us, the day was perfect, the approach was short, and we had the spot mostly to ourselves."
        %p= "We climbed three top rope routes, all with easy access to the anchors by walking up the back. You should be careful though - it seems people like to fish and drink there and have removed or loosened the hardware in the past - so be sure to check your anchors carefully."
        %p= "Half a dozen routes surround the massive boulder, and a spicy V4 traverse spans the bottom. I didn't try it because I didn't bring a swimming suit - if you fall the water is your crash pad. I definitely plan to revisit this spot when I get a chance"
        %p= "- Nat Baykova"
  %article.club-report
    %h3= "Yosemite June 24th, 2026"
    = link_to "View photos", "https://photos.app.goo.gl/u3WMAv9twTG1p3Ca9", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener"
    %details.club-report-details
      %summary Read trip report
      .club-report-copy
        %p= "We started out running laps on grant's crack (5.9) on swan slab in the valley. It's a short single pitch that starts with some easy slab on large knobs and then transitions into a low-angle finger crack. Hands are good, feet less so. A short scramble leads to a final push up more easy slab. Bolted anchors at the top. This was my first 5.9 lead in the valley!"
        %p= "Once you've built an anchor, you can use a BD #2 or #3 to set a redirect over the top rope routes to the right. We spent some time on unnamed thin crack (5.10), which after you stuff yourself into or lie back an offwidth chimney leads to an... unnamed thin crack with small fingers. I struggled quite a bit, always finding my feet way too close to my hands on questionable holds. Pearl crushed it. But she's better at crack than I am so that's to be expected. If you keep towards the right near the top you have the opportunity for some fun slab moves that end in a mantle up a dinner plate. I like slab and my fingers were blasted, so this was my favorite part."
        %p= "- Eric Schkufza"
        %p= "Fri"
        %p= "Arrive around midnight on Friday. Dave is exceptionally jetlagged and asleep in car."
        %p= "Sat"
        %p= "Slow start, arrive in crag parking lot around 11:45 am, hoping to climb in Church Bowl area. We circle a few times, no luck. Migrate to a different lot, eventually find a spot, go to Swan Slab Gully instead. Eric wants to lead Grant's Crack, which we ran on TR a few weeks before. Not yet clean but a great lead. Dave goes next on TR, his first climb in a while. I go last, clean the route, struggle to find good locks this time around."
        %p= "Eric TR's Grant's Crack again at my urging, and we set up a TR redirect for the unnamed 10A next door. Eric starts the 10A halfway up (from the blocky ledge), flails a bit. Dave is napping on a bench at this point. I start at the bottom and optimistically think I'll squeeze myself into the short chimney behind the ledge ... it's extremely dirty and the gear on my harness is too bulky. Switch to laybacking the arete instead of chimneying, then surprisingly manage to mostly cruise the section above (clean but with effort). Eric climbs the 10A again. I TR Grant's Crack 1x more (solid locks this time) and we call it a day."
        %p= "After dinner we get to meet a bunch of folks at the campfire -- lovely time and lovely chats! Dave C. was mostly asleep on his chair."
        %p= "Sun"
        %p= "We scout for a spot for Dave to paint in Tuolumne, settling on Tenaya Lake. Eric and I scramble, meander, and sunbathe nearby."
        %p= "Everyone had a blast!!"
        %p= "- Pearl Wu"
  %article.club-report
